{
  "_doc": [
    "How ledger.py assigns each Claude Code session and agent to a purpose (scopo) and an area.",
    "1. An agent whose description starts with a tag, e.g. '[Cybran] client models', gets scopo 'Cybran'.",
    "2. Otherwise the first rule in 'regole' whose text occurs in the description gives the scopo.",
    "3. Otherwise agents get 'default_agente', main sessions 'default_sessione' (or a 'sessioni' override).",
    "'aree' maps each scopo to its area; a scopo missing there shows up under 'Da classificare' in summary.org",
    "and is named at every session start until it gets one. 'aree_valide' are the only areas 'ledger.py tag' accepts.",
    "'onde' maps each module scopo to its wave (table 'Per onda' of summary.org); scopi without a wave (main sessions,",
    "documentation, planning) are counted as 'Fuori onda'.",
    "'righe' = lines the module added in src/, tests/, tools/, data/ when it merged into main: after a merge run",
    "  git diff --numstat <merge>^1 <merge> -- src tests tools data | awk '{a+=$1} END {print a}'",
    "and write the number here (sum the merges of a module merged in pieces). A module without 'righe' is in progress.",
    "Rules, areas, waves and lines also apply to ledger rows whose transcripts were already deleted.",
    "Edit this file, then run: python3 tools/token-ledger/ledger.py update"
  ],
